ot need an elephant, a smith, or a wall. It does not even need Sicily.\n\nStrip off the names, and you have a story you have already watched. A man is trapped by a giant, blinds him, and gets away.\n\nScholars have recorded more than two hundred versions. Iceland. Portugal. Russia. Even the Arabian Nights.\n\nMost scholars think the tale is older than Homer.\n\n\"So I was not the first,\" Odysseus muttered.\n\nThat does not rule out the skull. It does mean the story does not need one.\n\nOn that view, Homer did not invent the Cyclops story. He gave us the best-known version."}